{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788474629-LMEqa8jZMjAL6IO4Tt35","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything is done. Let me summarize the work.\n\nSummary of changes:\n1. `slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/internals.py` — `_to_authorize_result` now reads the `x-oauth-scopes` header from the auth.test response and passes it as `bot_scopes` for bot tokens (`xoxb-`) or `user_scopes` for user tokens. `AuthorizeResult.__init__` already converts the comma-separated header string into a list of scopes.\n2. `tests/mock_web_api_server.py` — mock auth.test responses now include `x-oauth-scopes` headers (bot: `chat:write,commands`, user: `chat:write,search:read`).\n3. New tests in both sync and async test files.\n\nSince both `SingleTeamAuthorization` and `AsyncSingleTeamAuthorization` funnel through `_to_authorize_result`, the single change covers both App and AsyncApp. Backward compat: only new fields added; existing fields unchanged; when the header is absent, scopes are None as before.\n\nTest results: 8/8 middleware tests, 22/22 authorize tests, full suite 634 passed (excluding adapter_tests which fail to import due to missing optional deps — pre-existing).","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02e22cc0-e01a-43f1-b698-3e20536e0a1c","uuid":"4c98ef3a-01e0-430e-b030-bc79f6469781","timestamp":"2026-09-03T22:30:35.516Z","request_id":"gen-1788474629-LMEqa8jZMjAL6IO4Tt35"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788474629-LMEqa8jZMjAL6IO4Tt35","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All tasks complete — the full test suite passes (634 passed).\n\n## Summary\n\n`SingleTeamAuthorization` (and `AsyncSingleTeamAuthorization`) both build their `AuthorizeResult` through the shared `_to_authorize_result` helper, so a single change covers both `slack_bolt.App` and `slack_bolt.async_app.AsyncApp`:\n\n**`slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/internals.py:71-81`** — `_to_authorize_result` now reads the `x-oauth-scopes` header from the `auth.test` response and routes it by token type:\n```python\noauth_scopes: Optional[str] = auth_test_result.headers.get(\"x-oauth-scopes\")\n...\nbot_scopes=oauth_scopes if _is_bot_token(token) else None,\nuser_scopes=None if _is_bot_token(token) else oauth_scopes,\n```\n`AuthorizeResult.__init__` already splits the comma-separated header string into a list, so `authorize_result.bot_scopes` arrives as `[\"chat:write\", \"commands\"]`.\n\n**Test support:**\n- `tests/mock_web_api_server.py` — mock `auth.test` responses now emit `x-oauth-scopes` headers (bot: `chat:write,commands`; user: `chat:write,search:read`), matching real Slack API behavior.\n- New `test_success_pattern_with_bot_scopes` in both `tests/slack_bolt/middleware/authorization/` and `tests/slack_bolt_async/middleware/authorization/`.\n\n**Backward compatibility:** only two new attributes are added to the authorize result; every existing field is untouched. When the header is absent, scopes are `None` — no existing behavior changes.\n\n**Verified:** bot tokens (`xoxb-`) populate `bot_scopes` with `user_scopes` as `None`; user tokens (`xoxp-`) populate `user_scopes` with `bot_scopes` as `None` — confirmed live through both the sync and async middlewares, plus end-to-end via `App`. The full suite passes: 634 passed (the excluded `tests/adapter_tests*` modules fail at import on missing optional deps like `chalice`, which is pre-existing and unrelated).\n\nOne usage note: since these values come from the `auth.test` response headers, they reflect whatever token the single-team app was configured with — so for an `xoxb-` token you'll always see `bot_scopes` populated and `user_scopes` as `None`, which is what you'd want when gating features on bot-token grants.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02e22cc0-e01a-43f1-b698-3e20536e0a1c","uuid":"fd5f169d-1bc4-418f-a867-1c3c0b408d33","timestamp":"2026-09-03T22:30:41.986Z","request_id":"gen-1788474629-LMEqa8jZMjAL6IO4Tt35"}
